    The minimum cost would be the minimum of the given possibilities,
    cost(10, 20, 30, 40) = min(cost(10) + cost(20, 30, 40), cost(10, 20) + cost(30, 40), cost(10, 20, 30) + cost(40))

    More preciesly in the terms of indices,
    cost(i, j) = cost(i, k) + cost(k, j)

    So we have to take the values of all the possibilities in order to get the result as well.
